}

// Exercises 2, Ex 8(c) | relation-properties | difficulty 1
::ex2-8-sym::[html]A binary relation r on A is symmetric if and only if\: {
    ~(a, a) ∈ r for every a ∈ A#Incorrect
    =(a, b) ∈ r implies (b, a) ∈ r#Correct
    ~(a, b) ∈ r and (b, a) ∈ r imply a \= b#Incorrect
    ~(a, b) ∈ r and (b, c) ∈ r imply (a, c) ∈ r#Incorrect
}

// Exercises 3, Ex 1(e) | functions-rel | difficulty 2
::ex3-1-fn::[html]Which of these relations r ⊆ R × R is a function from R to R? {
    ~x r y \: x² + y² \= 1#Incorrect
    ~x r y \: x \= y²#Incorrect
    =x r y \: y \= eˣ#Correct
    ~x r y \: |x − y| \= 1#Incorrect
}

// Exercises 3, Ex 8(d) | functions-rel | difficulty 2
::ex3-8-chi::[html]For the characteristic function χX of a set X ⊆ U, what is χ(A∩B)(x) equal to? {
    ~χA(x) + χB(x)#Incorrect
    =χA(x) · χB(x)#Correct
    ~χA(x) − χB(x)#Incorrect
    ~χA(x) + χB(x) − χA(x) · χB(x)#Incorrect
}

// Exercises 4, Ex 9 | ordering-relations | difficulty 2
::ex4-9-well::[html]Why is ⟨Z, ≤⟩ NOT a well-ordering? {
    ~≤ is not linear on Z#Incorrect
    =Z has non-empty subsets (e.g. Z itself) with no smallest element#Correct
    ~Some pairs of integers are incomparable under ≤#Incorrect
    ~≤ is not transitive on Z#Incorrect
}

