// Exercises 13, Ex 11(3) | quantifiers, predicate | difficulty 2
::ex13-11-all::[html]Let K(x, y) mean "x knows y". Which formula says "Everyone knows everyone"? {
    =∀x∀y K(x, y)#Correct
    ~∃x∃y K(x, y)#Incorrect
    ~∀x∃y K(x, y)#Incorrect
    ~∃x∀y K(x, y)#Incorrect
}

// Exercises 13, Ex 11(2) | quantifiers, predicate | difficulty 3
::ex13-11-notall::[html]Let K(x, y) mean "x knows y". Which formula says "Not everyone knows someone"? {
    =¬∀x∃y K(x, y)#Correct
    ~∀x∃y K(x, y)#Incorrect
    ~∀x¬∃y K(x, y)#Incorrect
    ~∃y∀x ¬K(x, y)#Incorrect
}

